// Title: Suspicious Processes Spawned by WinRM
// Sigma ID: 5cc2cda8-f261-4d88-a2de-e9e193c86716
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Andreas Hunkeler (@Karneades), Markus Neis
// Date: 2021-05-20 | Modified: 2022-07-14
// ATT&CK: T1190, initial-access, persistence, privilege-escalation
// Description: Detects suspicious processes including shells spawnd from WinRM host process
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate WinRM usage
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_winrm_susp_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\wsmprovhost.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\sh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\bash.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wsl.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\schtasks.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\certutil.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\whoami.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\bitsadmin.exe")
